MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Echo Show 8 feels like a useful addition because its screen could support video calling and viewing compatible camera feeds alongside my home electronics.",
    "The smart plug offers a new convenience: controlling a lamp by voice fits naturally with my Alexa-enabled devices."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "More Fire TV sticks repeat a purpose already served by my 4K stick and Fire TV television; an HD version or themed remote cover gives me no clear reason to buy again.",
    "The tablet and charging cables do not address a current need. My television and camera purchases do not imply that I need a tablet or own devices requiring those cables."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to keep offering similar streaming devices, even though I already have that function covered.",
    "Interest in home electronics seems to have been stretched into interest in almost any Amazon device or electronic accessory, regardless of what it would help me do."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent Blink purchase makes another camera less urgent, even though home monitoring remains relevant to me.",
    "I am more interested in adding a useful capability than duplicating equipment. I would choose the larger Echo Show 8 for easier viewing, without also needing the Show 5 or a separate speaker."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in connected home entertainment and cameras, but often confused that interest with a need for more devices serving the same purpose."
}
